  "response_text": "I rewrote `merge_intervals` in `app/intervals.py` to meet the contract. The public check passes (2/2), and so do 14 new tests I added in `app/test_intervals.py`.\n\n**Changes**\n- **Validation:** every pair is checked first, and any `start > end` raises `ValueError`, even when other intervals are empty.\n- **Empty intervals:** pairs with `start == end` are dropped.\n- **Merging:** intervals are sorted and merged when they overlap or touch (`start <= previous end`).\n- **Input:** the input is consumed once into a new list and never modified, so generators work.\n- **Standard library only.**\n\n**Tests**\n- Public check: `python -m unittest discover -s . -p 'test_public.py' -v` → 2 tests, OK.\n- My tests: `python -m unittest discover -s . -p 'test_intervals.py' -v` → 14 tests, OK. They cover overlap, touching, gaps, nesting, duplicates, negative coordinates, empty intervals, reversed bounds, generators, input preservation, empty input, and output ordering.\n\n`test_public.py` is at the repo root, not inside `app/`, and I left it unchanged.",
